# Arguments of feosd (feosd.service). For example, to serve the API on TCP
# too, without authentication, for a lab:
#
#   FEOSD_ARGS="--tcp [::]:1337"
#
# Pods have an IPv6 address on the network and an IPv4 address for
# leaving this node through masquerade (ADR 0010). feosd needs the prefix
# that the network routes to this node to give pods a network; without it,
# pods with a network fail:
#
#   --pod-prefix PREFIX       e.g. 2001:db8:7:1::/64. A /64 is best, a
#                             smaller one such as a /80 is enough. A lab
#                             whose network routes nothing to the node takes
#                             a ULA, such as fd00:fe05:1::/64: its pods leave
#                             over IPv4 alone, and nothing outside the node
#                             reaches them.
#   --pod-ipv4-range PREFIX   the pods' IPv4 addresses, a /32 each,
#                             169.254.16.0/20 by default.
#   --dns-address ADDRESS     the pods' resolver, an IPv4 address this node
#                             holds, 169.254.0.53 by default. The pods'
#                             gateway is 169.254.0.1, which the node answers
#                             ARP for on their TAP devices and never holds.
#                             feosd.socket holds the resolver's sockets
#                             across restarts of feosd: another address
#                             needs a drop-in for it too, as the unit says.
#   --dns-upstream ADDRESS    a resolver it asks for pods that name none
#                             (repeatable); Google's and Cloudflare's by
#                             default.
#   --deny-prefix PREFIX      a prefix of either family that no pod reaches
#                             (repeatable): the control plane, management
#                             networks. Link-local addresses, such as a
#                             cloud's metadata service, and this node's own
#                             are denied always.
#
# A lab:
#
#   FEOSD_ARGS="--pod-prefix fd00:fe05:1::/64 --deny-prefix 10.0.0.0/8"
#
# With a control plane (ADR 0015), feosd joins it once with a join token
# from its operator and then connects to every instance of it. Without
# --control-plane, the node is on its own.
#
#   --control-plane HOST:PORT   the control plane's port for nodes, which
#                               the join dials, e.g. 10.43.0.17:7443.
#   --control-plane-name NAME   the DNS name of the control plane's
#                               certificate, checked wherever feosd dials;
#                               HOST by default, needed when HOST is an
#                               address.
#   --trust-domain NAME         the control plane's SPIFFE trust domain,
#                               feos.local by default.
#   --join-token-file PATH      the join token, feos-join-<secret>.<pin>,
#                               readable by root alone; /etc/feos/join-token
#                               by default. It is read until the node has
#                               joined, and again when the control plane
#                               removed the node.
#   --node-dir PATH             the node's key, certificate and trust
#                               bundle, /var/lib/feos/node by default.
#
#   FEOSD_ARGS="--control-plane 10.43.0.17:7443 --control-plane-name ferun.example.com --trust-domain run.example.com"
FEOSD_ARGS=""
